# Saturn.jl (saturn-stage)

Julia implementation and benchmark suite for the **Saturn coefficient**, an unsupervised metric designed to evaluate both local and global structure preservation in UMAP dimensionality reduction.

Based on the paper:
> Davide Chicco, Simone Melzi, Francesca Gasparini, and Giuseppe Jurman (2026). *The advantages of our proposed Saturn coefficient over continuity and trustworthiness for UMAP dimensionality reduction evaluation*. PeerJ Computer Science, 12:e3424. DOI: [10.7717/peerj-cs.3424](https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj-cs.3424)

## Project Structure
Organized according to Noble (2009) and Schnell (2015) guidelines:
- `data/`: Standardized CSV test inputs (`input_data.csv`, `umap_output_layout.csv`) and target Ground Truth values (`target_score.txt`).
- `scripts/`: Python benchmark scripts to generate deterministic reference datasets.
- `src/`: Core Julia implementation (`Saturn.jl`).
- `test/`: Automated test suite comparing Julia outputs against Python reference calculations.

